 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<p>The method is yours; these details are my guesses — adjust and tell me: <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> oil</b> for the ginger; marinating <b>15–30 min</b>; the <b>kombu goes into the pan</b> with the marinade and comes out before the egg; the pan cools <b>~5 min</b> off the heat before the chicken goes in.</p>",
   "title_html": "Filled in from your description"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cook the breast in the bath first (<a href=\"sous-vide.html#chicken-breast\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"63\" data-s=\"0\">63 °C</span>, 60–75 min for ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 cm</span></a>), then slice it.</li><li>Skip marinating: after the ginger and onion (step 5), pour in the sauce, bring it to a simmer and add the cooked chicken for just <b>1 minute</b> — no longer, or it tightens — then go straight to the egg.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Sous vide chicken shortcut"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Homemade is best — see <a href=\"niboshi-bonito-dashi.html\">niboshi–bonito dashi</a>.</li><li>Water plus <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.25\" data-s=\"0\">¼ tsp</span> dashi powder is the quick version; the kombu in the marinade adds depth either way.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Dashi"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The eggs end up only just set.</li><li>If anyone eating should avoid undercooked egg, keep the lid on with the heat low for another minute or two until fully set.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Soft eggs"
  }
 ],
