 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Have a bowl of hot rice ready before you start the pan — the egg won’t wait.</li><li>Start the rice cooker about 45 minutes ahead, or reheat leftover rice until steaming.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Rice first",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Scoop the hot rice in loosely with a damp paddle — don't press it down.",
      "src": "illustrations/oyakodon/1-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/oyakodon/1.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~45 min ahead",
   "time_html": "<span>~45 min ahead</span>",
   "title": "Rice first",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-f=\"bowl|bowls\" data-n=\"1\">1 bowl</span>",
     "name_html": "Cooked short-grain rice"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Trim the thigh fillets of any excess fat and cut them into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"2\" data-b=\"3\" data-s=\"0\">2–3 cm</span> pieces.</li><li>In a bowl, stir until the sugar dissolves:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>dashi <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"80\">80 ml</span></span></li><li>soy sauce <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"4\">4 tbsp</span></span></li><li>mirin <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span></span></li><li>sake <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span></span></li><li>sugar <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span></span></li></ul></li><li>Drop in the kombu, then the chicken.</li><li>Leave it 15–30 minutes (in the fridge if longer).</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Marinate the chicken",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Trim off excess fat, then cut the thigh into 2–3 cm pieces.",
      "src": "illustrations/oyakodon/2-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Stir soy, mirin, sake and sugar into the dashi until the sugar dissolves; add the kombu, then the chicken.",
      "src": "illustrations/oyakodon/2-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/oyakodon/2.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~5 min + 15–30 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min + 15–30 min</span>",
   "title": "Marinate the chicken",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"150\">150 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Chicken thigh fillets"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "a <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 cm</span> square",
     "name_html": "Kombu"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Onion: cut off both ends (root and tip), halve it through the cut ends and peel.</li><li>Lay each half flat and slice it <b>lengthwise — perpendicular to the cut ends</b>, along the lines — about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 mm</span> thick. Slicing across the lines gives rings that fall apart; lengthwise slices hold their shape in the pan.</li><li>Ginger: peel, cut into thin matchsticks, then across into <b>tiny cubes</b>.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Onion and ginger",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Onion: cut off both ends — root and tip — then halve it through the cut ends and peel.",
      "src": "illustrations/oyakodon/3-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Slice lengthwise — perpendicular to the cut ends, along the lines — about 5 mm.",
      "src": "illustrations/oyakodon/3-how2.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Ginger: peel with a spoon edge, slice thin, cut into matchsticks, then across into tiny cubes.",
      "src": "illustrations/oyakodon/3-how3.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/oyakodon/3.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Onion and ginger",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-n=\"1\">½</span> small (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"60\">60 g</span>)",
     "name_html": "Onion"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "a <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 cm</span> piece (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"8\">8 g</span>)",
     "name_html": "Ginger"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Crack the eggs into a bowl and beat <b>loosely — 4–5 strokes with chopsticks</b>, cutting through the whites.</li><li>You want streaks of white and yolk, not a uniform yellow.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Beat the eggs",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Beat loosely — 4–5 quick strokes, cutting through the whites. Stop while streaks remain.",
      "src": "illustrations/oyakodon/4-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/oyakodon/4.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~1 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min</span>",
   "title": "Beat the eggs",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"2\" data-n=\"1\">2</span>",
     "name_html": "Eggs"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Small pan, the oil, medium-low heat.</li><li>Drop in the ginger for ~30 seconds until fragrant, then add the onion and a pinch of salt.</li><li>Stir until the onion is <b>a bit soft</b> — 2–3 minutes, no colour.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "label_html": "<span>medium-low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Ginger, then onion",
